{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2143","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2143","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2143\",\"parent_revision\":\"467a53a475da3665e1bebc14a2943b3eac72ba69\",\"root_revision\":\"241ea2f14e8719cc5ab644d8c5452cd4da9d4cb23267ee8d081cf8cc1af395ee\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Condition | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | PRESENT | Persist `result_summary` on completion; inject parent summaries into child prompts |\\n| Scope boundaries | PRESENT | `Task` model + `start-task` skill + `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler; backward-compatible |\\n| External interfaces | PRESENT | `sam_task(action='state')`, `sam_task(action='read')`, `update_fields`, `TaskAssignment`, hook stdin JSON |\\n| Existing system context | PRESENT | `Task` model verified at `models.py:118`; `handoff: str = \\\"\\\"` at line 214; `TaskAssignment` at line 477; `StateTaskConfig` at `action_models.py:112` |\\n| Constraints | DERIVABLE | Byte budget 2000 chars/parent from Cursor Cookbook reference; configurable per description; `StateTaskConfig` has no `result_summary` param yet |\\n| Verification expectations | PRESENT | Measurable signal with exact test command provided in item |\\n\\n**Gap**: `StateTaskConfig` (action_models.py line 112) has no `result_summary` field \u2014 must be added. The `handoff` field (models.py line 214) exists but is free-form and unpopulated by tooling; `result_summary` is a distinct, hook-populated field. Gap is implementation-detail level, not a planning blocker.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **persist task result_summary and inject parent outputs into child task prompts** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/cursor-cookbook.md \u2014 pattern: Parent Result Injection (DAG Task Runner)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-08)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 DAG-based parallel tasks currently have no structured handoff channel. Each child agent re-derives parent outputs via git diff or filesystem inspection, wasting context budget and causing divergence. This directly degrades SAM pipeline quality for any multi-task plan with data-flow dependencies.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: child task agents that depend on parent task outputs (any SAM plan with `dependencies:` between tasks)\\n- Bottleneck: tasks requiring knowledge of what a parent task produced (e.g., T2 needing T1's schema decisions) must re-read all changed files from scratch\\n- Affects: `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler, `start-task` skill, `sam_task(action='state')` call path, `sam_task(action='read')` response shape via `TaskAssignment`\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Child agents receive a structured 2000-char snippet of parent results without filesystem inspection\\n- Eliminates redundant codebase re-reads across task boundaries, reducing context consumption\\n- Provides an audit trail of what each task produced (visible in plan YAML)\\n- Enables downstream tasks to make decisions based on upstream decisions without re-analyzing all changed files\\n- Backward-compatible: empty `result_summary` means the injected section is omitted\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a task transitions to `complete`, its `result_summary` field is populated with a structured summary of what the task produced. When a downstream task is started via `start-task`, its prompt context includes a \\\"Parent Task Outputs\\\" section listing the `result_summary` of every completed dependency task, truncated to a configurable byte budget (default 2000 chars/parent). When dependencies are absent or `result_summary` is empty, the section is omitted and the behavior is identical to current.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `Task` model gains `result_summary: str = \\\"\\\"` field with `serialization_alias=\\\"result-summary\\\"` matching existing field conventions\\n- `StateTaskConfig` in `action_models.py` gains an optional `result_summary: str | None = None` field\\n- `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler populates `result_summary` during completion (via `sam_update_plan_fields` or equivalent)\\n- `start-task` SKILL.md gains a step (after step 1a artifact load) that reads `result_summary` from each dependency task via `sam_task(action='read')` and prepends a \\\"Parent Task Outputs\\\" section to the agent's context\\n- The byte budget is configurable (env var or plan-level field) with a default of 2000 chars per parent\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run python -c \\\"from sam_schema.core.models import Task; t = Task(id='T01', title='x', status='complete', result_summary='foo'); print(t.model_dump()['result-summary'])\\\"` prints `foo` without error\\n2. `sam_task(action='state', status='complete', result_summary='...')` persists the value to the plan YAML `result-summary` field on the task\\n3. `sam_task(action='read')` for a task whose dependencies have non-empty `result_summary` returns a `TaskAssignment` where the agent context (or a new field) includes a \\\"Parent Task Outputs\\\" section\\n4. `start-task` skill step reads dependency `result_summary` fields and prepends the section to the working context when at least one dependency has a non-empty value\\n5. When all dependency `result_summary` fields are empty or there are no dependencies, `start-task` omits the section with no error\\n6. Existing tests pass: `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/ -x`\\n7. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` exits 0\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` (Task model line 118, handoff field line 214, TaskAssignment line 477) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` (StateTaskConfig line 112, UpdateTaskConfig line 126) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` (update_plan_fields line 119, get_task_assignment line 228) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` (SubagentStop handler line 952, sam_update_status call line 1013) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` (task loading steps 1\u20132a, lines 43\u201390) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` (sam_task tool, state case line 627, read case line 593) |\\n| Prior art | `research/agent-frameworks/cursor-cookbook.md` lines 86\u201390 \u2014 DAG Task Runner \\\"Parent Result Injection\\\" pattern (2000-char snippet) |\\n| Test suite | `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/` \u2014 existing integration tests for sam_task read/state actions |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None identified \u2014 `Task` model, hook, and skill are independently modifiable\\n- Blocks: Any downstream item that assumes `result_summary` exists on `Task` (none currently identified in backlog)\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone \u2014 RT-ICA APPROVED-WITH-GAPS. The single gap (adding `result_summary` to `StateTaskConfig`) is a straightforward model extension with no external dependencies.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Three touch-points: (1) add field to `Task` model + `StateTaskConfig`, (2) update `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler to write it, (3) update `start-task` SKILL.md to inject parent outputs. All are well-scoped. Existing `update_fields` and `sam_update_plan_fields` mechanisms handle the write path. Risk: ensuring the 2000-char truncation is applied consistently and the section is correctly omitted when empty.\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: `./research/agent-frameworks/cursor-cookbook.md` \u2014 DAG Task Runner pattern: \\\"Automatically stitches upstream output into child task prompts (2,000-char snippet of parent results)\\\" (Key Features section, lines 86-90 of the entry).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe `Task` Pydantic model at `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py:114` defines fields for status, dependencies, timestamps, content (description/objective/requirements), and `handoff: str = \\\"\\\"` (line 210), but has no field that captures the structured output or result summary of a completed task in a form retrievable by downstream tasks. When `start-task` (at `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md:43-72`) loads a task assignment, it reads `plan.goal`, `plan.context`, and the task itself via `sam_task(action='read')`, plus the architect spec via `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")`. There is no step that retrieves the completed-state output of dependency tasks (`task.dependencies`) and injects a summary snippet into the new agent's prompt. Each task agent therefore re-derives or re-reads what its parents produced from scratch, or relies on filesystem inspection of git diffs without a structured handoff.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe `Task` model gains a `result_summary: str` field (with serialization alias `result-summary`, sized to a configurable byte budget) populated by the `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler (or by an explicit `sam_task(action='state', status='complete', result_summary=...)` call) when a task transitions to `complete`. The `start-task` workflow at step 1a or 2a inserts a new step that reads the `result_summary` of every entry in `task.dependencies` via `sam_task(action='read')` and prepends a \\\"Parent Task Outputs\\\" section to the agent's working context with each truncated to a configurable byte budget (e.g. 2000 chars per parent, matching the Cursor Cookbook DAG Task Runner pattern). When dependencies are absent or `result_summary` is empty, the section is omitted (backward compatible).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAfter implementation, run:\\n\\n```bash\\nuv run python -c \\\"from sam_schema.core.models import Task; t = Task(id='T01', title='x', status='complete', result_summary='foo'); print(t.model_dump()['result-summary'])\\\"\\n```\\n\\nOutput includes `result-summary: foo`. Then in a SAM plan with two tasks where T02 depends on T01: dispatching T02 via `start-task` produces an agent prompt whose context includes a section labeled \\\"Parent Task Outputs\\\" containing T01's `result_summary` truncated to the configured limit. Verify by reading the JSONL session file for the T02 agent and grep for the parent-output section header.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"efeb40e6f7dc675db6f266110de456abb5bff113db7e3ebe4f14daa8ffcba95d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPuhfjQ\"}"}